## Array methods

| Method | Returns | Mutates original? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `map` | new array | No |
| `filter` | new array | No |
| `reduce` | accumulated value | No |
| `sort` | sorted array | Yes |
| `splice` | removed items | Yes |

## Async/await

```js
async function getUser(id) {
  const res = await fetch(`/api/users/${id}`);
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Not found');
  return res.json();
}
```

## Destructuring

```js
const { title, language, summary } = cheatsheet;
const [first, ...rest] = items;
```

## Big-O quick reference

Average time complexity of common operations, where $n$ is the input size:

- Array access: $O(1)$
- Linear search: $O(n)$
- Binary search: $O(\log n)$
- Sorting (comparison-based): $O(n \log n)$
